Round 1 (2026-02-26)

What changed
- Files changed: `clang/aot/_.c`, `clang/aot/emit.c`.
- Replaced fallback env capture model (`const Term args[]`) with live bind-list heads:
  - `aot_fallback_alo(tm_loc, len, ls_loc)` now directly returns `term_new_alo(ls_loc, len, tm_loc)`.
  - No per-fallback re-encoding of binders from plain `xN` terms.
- Emitter now tracks lexical env as real bind nodes (`eN`) in compiled code.
  - LAM binders (`head` LAM and expr APP-LAM path) allocate `eN=[SUB(xN), prev]`.
  - DUP binders always compile (removed static-only guard), still capped by `AOT_ENV_CAP`.
  - DUP binder cell policy:
    - if `aot_is_copy_free(xN)`: store `SUB(xN)` (resolved immediately),
    - else: store raw `xN` (pending DUP cell).
- DP/BJ variable emission now observes live DUP state via `eN`:
  - read `cell = heap_read(eN + 0)`;
  - if `cell` has SUB bit: use substituted payload;
  - else emit `DP0/DP1` term with same label and loc=`eN`.
- Fallback expressions now use current env head (`e{dep-1}`) and preserve pending vs substituted DUP state.
- Removed now-unneeded static copy-free recursion helpers from emitter.

Semantic notes
- This mirrors `wnf` linked DUP behavior better: DUP state is represented as a mutable cell, not only as a captured value.
- Sharing is preserved between compiled terms and deopted residual ALO terms because both reference the same live env-chain nodes.
- DUP introduction no longer increments interaction count in the emitter path.

Critical pitfalls found
- Deterministic `--as-c` temp path collides across parallel runs; this caused misleading diagnostics during debugging.
  - Always run AOT checks sequentially; kill stale `test/_all_.sh` runs before targeted `--as-c` repros.
- After emitter edits, stale `clang/main` can make debugging look inconsistent; always rebuild before interpreting generated C.
- Codegen scope bug: declaring `Term <out>` inside both branches of emitted `if` made `<out>` undefined after the block.
  - Fix pattern: declare once before `if`, assign in branches.

Validation done
- Rebuilt: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`.
- Full suite: `./test/_all_.sh` passed (interpreted + AOT).
- Bench parity checks:
  - `../bench/bench/gab_deriv/main.hvm`: hvmi vs hvmc outputs match.
  - `../bench/bench/gen_easy/main.hvm -C1`: hvmi vs hvmc outputs match.

Current state
- AOT no longer bails out at DUP just because value is non-static/non-copy-free.
- Compiled mode now carries dynamic DUP binder state through env cells and deopts without losing that state.
- This is foundational correctness plumbing; it increases compiled coverage across DUP-heavy case trees.

Remaining limitations
- Many strict contexts still eventually delegate DUP interactions to normal runtime reduction when a `DP0/DP1` term is forced.
- Large speedups likely require compiling more of the DP interaction frontier directly (not only preserving state through deopt).

Next likely step
- Add compiled handling for forced DP interactions in strict/head contexts (mirror `wnf` DP-frame dispatch: DUP-NAM/LAM/SUP/NOD), reusing runtime helpers where safe, to reduce wnf fallback pressure on DUP-heavy hot paths.
